# Holding Next Tab (⌥⌘↓) and letting go stops where the key was let go. A tab switch can hold the main
# thread for 30–100 ms and more while macOS repeats a held key every 33–83 ms, so repeats queued behind
# slow switches and played out after the key came up, walking on for several tabs and loading each one.
# A repeat older than one and a half repeat intervals is dropped (KeyRepeatGate). Ten Today tabs (the
# newest first), the fifth selected; one press and five repeats a second old: one tab down, no further.
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
pace 0.5
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
repeat 10 cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=tab${i}x
wait 2
cra://debug?selectTab=n=tab5x
wait 1
cra://debug?selectedTab=start
expect-log selected tab start: \S+\?n=tab5x$
cra://debug?key=%EF%9C%81,125,1572864
repeat 5 cra://debug?key=%EF%9C%81,125,1572864&repeat=1&age=1000
wait 1.5
cra://debug?selectedTab=held
expect-log selected tab held: \S+\?n=tab4x$
